 61MN    U(P,X):ISOTOPE SHIFT:XUNDL-6  2016HE14                           201612
 61MN c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2016He14:                          
 61MN c  Phys Rev C 94, 054321 (2016)                                           
 61MN c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL/MSU), December 8, 2010                       
 61MN c  2016He14: E=1.4 GeV proton beam was produced from the ISOLDE facility  
 61MN2c  at CERN. Target was a thick uranium carbide. Recoiling ions were       
 61MN3c  ionized using the resonance ionization laser ion source (RILIS),       
 61MN4c  mass-separated, cooled and bunched in the gas-filled RFQ ISCOOL,       
 61MN5c  re-accelerated and guided to the laser spectroscopy beam line COLLAPS. 
 61MN6c  Measured hyperfine spectra using collinear laser spectroscopy on atomic
 61MN7c  and ionic transitions, respectively. Deduced changes in mean-square    
 61MN8c  charge radii relative to {+55}Mn. Comparisons with theoretical         
 61MN9c  calculations. Systematics of neighboring nuclei.                       
 61MN cL J,T$From Adopted Levels of {+61}Mn in ENSDF database.                  
